---
title: Thai jungle curry with chicken
servings: 4
tags: [chicken, gluten-free, dairy-free]
cuisine: thai
time: 50 minutes
source: Thai Jungle Curry with Chicken by Pailin Chongchitnant, Hot Thai Kitchen, https://hot-thai-kitchen.com/jungle-curry
---

== Quick curry paste ==

Pound the @green Thai chilies{3}(seeded for less heat) fine in a #mortar and pestle{}. Add @fingerroot{2%tbsp}(chopped) and @lemongrass{2%tbsp}(thinly sliced) and pound to a fine paste.

Pound in the @red curry paste{4-5%tbsp}.

> The paste keeps a few days in the fridge or a few months frozen.

== From-scratch curry paste (instead) ==

Grind the @?mild dried chilies{0.7%oz}(such as guajillo or puya) to a powder in a spice grinder.

In a heavy mortar, pound the @?green Thai chilies{3-5}, @?coarse salt{1%tsp} and @?white peppercorns{1/4%tsp} fine.

Add @?lemongrass{1%stalk}(bottom half, thinly sliced), @?galangal{1%tbsp}(finely chopped), @?fingerroot{1%tbsp}(finely chopped), @?makrut lime zest{1%tsp}(finely chopped) and @?cilantro roots{1%tsp}(or stems, finely chopped). Pound fine, then pound in the ground chilies.

Add @?shallots{3%tbsp}(finely chopped) and @?garlic{1%tbsp}(finely chopped) and pound fine. Pound in the @?fermented shrimp paste{1%tsp}.

== Curry ==

Fry the curry paste in the @neutral oil{2%tbsp} in a #heavy-bottomed pot{} over medium heat ~{2%minutes}.

Toss in the @chicken thighs{12%oz}(boneless, skinless, cut into strips). Add the @chicken stock{2 1/2%cups}(unsalted) and simmer gently ~{15%minutes} until tender.

Stir in the @palm sugar{2%tsp} and @fish sauce{1-2%tbsp}. Add the @long beans{4.2%oz}(2-inch pieces), @baby corn{8}(bite-sized pieces), @Thai eggplant{4}(cut into 4 or 6 wedges), @?young green peppercorns{2%stems}, @?fingerroot{1/4%cup}(julienned) and @makrut lime leaves{4-5}. Simmer a few minutes until the vegetables are done.

Off the heat, stir in the @spur chilies{2}(julienned; or bell pepper), @holy basil leaves{1%cup} and @toasted rice powder{1 1/2%tbsp} so the basil just wilts. Season with more @fish sauce{}.

Serve with jasmine rice.
